huart->hdmarx->XferHalfCpltCallback = UART_DMARxHalfCplt;
Although it brings a warning of UART_DMARxHalfCplt, it works normally and can receive odd byte lengths normally.
The issue is not related to the above content, but rather the calling of the callback function in the UART_DMARxHalfCplt function, which informed me of the incorrect received length. By commenting it out, the HAL library proceeded to the UART_DMAReceiveCplt function and correctly returned the actual received length.

